  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Let the system of linear equations</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8211;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>13</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#955;</mi></math></p><p>has a unique solution <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#947;</mi></math>. Then the distance of the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#947;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> from the plane <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#955;</mi></math> is</p>"
  },
